@startuml
!include style.iuml
title Sequential robot homing · lifetime, deadlines and cleanup
caption The same StepperMotor seek/release/re-latch path is used for individual axis homing.
footer Software behavior; disconnected-board fixtures use synthetic reference switches.
autonumber
box "M7 · UI" #EDF4FE
participant "Client / Robot" as C
end box
boundary "Serialized ICC" as W #FFF5DF
box "M4 · IO" #EAF7F4
participant "Server" as S
participant "Controller\nexecution worker" as O
participant "StepperMotor\nselected stage" as M
participant "Runtime\nThreadX" as T
end box
C -> W : Acquire Robot ownership; Prepare Home; Run
W -> S : deferred preparation / action
S -> O : validate version, reservation, revisions, configuration
O -> O : store order and per-axis limits\nretain whole-robot ownership
S -> O : startProgram(completion callback)
O -> O : arm overall timeout if supplied
S --> W : accepted
W --> C : Running
loop Configured homing order, while no cancellation / fault / timeout
  O -> M : reference(seek, latch, stage timeout)
  M -> M : join previous worker before reusing its stack
  M -> T : create_jthread with reserved stack\n10 KiB ARM / 16 KiB Linux, priority 16
  note over M,T
    Stack storage is reserved once per motor.
    Thread control / TLS still need bounded runtime resources.
    Creation failures are logged with motor and job identity.
  end note
  M --> O : future<Result>; attach completion notification
  M -> M : seek contact → release → slow re-latch
  opt Overall timeout / owner lease expiry / cancellation
    O -> M : requestStop() for participating motors
    O -> O : record specific terminal reason\nwait for active-stage completion; do not start next stage
  end
  alt Successful latch
    M -> M : establish configured reference position
  else Stop / stage timeout / local fault
    M -> M : stop output; retain unsuccessful reference state
  end
  M -->> O : ready flag + notification
  O -> M : get completed result; stopAndWait()
  M --> O : worker joined and cleanup complete
  O -> O : advance only after successful stage
end
O -->> S : bounded completion record + notification
S -> W : terminal Completed / Stopped / Faulted
S -> O : releaseJob() after cleanup
W --> C : retained job history; notify explicit waiters
note over C,O #FFF5DF
  Interrupting motion wait does not cancel motion.
  A stop or timeout never resumes automatically.
  Only completed homing stages establish references.
end note
@enduml
